.TH FILES 1
.SH NAME
files \- file manager on ui(4)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B files
[
.I dir
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Files
shows one directory in a new window of
.IR ui (4),
.I dir
or the current one at the start.
Its path is in a text box at the top; a path typed there (absolute, or
relative to the directory shown) and enter go to it,
.B up
to the parent,
.B home
to
.BR $home .
Below are the directory's entries, its directories first (with a
.BR / ),
then its files with their sizes, each part by name.
.PP
A click on an entry selects it (shown with a
.BR » );
a second click on it, or
.BR open ,
opens it: a directory is gone into, a file's name is sent to the
.IR plumber (4)
from the directory shown, as a click of button 3 in
.IR acme (1)
does: the rules decide what opens it.
With an entry selected, the text box beside
.B open
holds its name:
.B rename
(or enter) gives it the name typed there, a name in the same directory
(as
.IR stat (5)'s
wstat renames).
.B Delete
asks first
.RB ( yes
or
.BR no );
a directory is deleted only when empty.
A name typed into the box at the bottom and
.B make
(or enter) make a new directory there.
The last line counts the entries and says what was done last, or what failed.
.PP
The directory is read again every 2 seconds: what other programs make,
change or take away there shows.
.PP
The window's files are those of
.IR ui (4):
.B /srv/ui.\fIuser\fP.\fIpid\fP.0
mounted elsewhere shows its tree; each entry is a button whose
.B text
is its name.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/files
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR ui (4),
.IR uiview (2),
.IR plumb (6),
.IR ls (1)
.SH BUGS
No copying or moving into another directory, and no selection of more
than one file.
